,"requests":6}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"de611fa4723a9c22f03cce205d36096f683b3f1b927681a4ca1375773e3cccdd"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":97660,"output_tokens":4056,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the counter and vectoring outcome when a retried `digest_unparsed` reply is recovered on the second attempt but yields an all-empty mapping (e.g. define 'succeeds' as 'recovers a mapping with ≥1 non-empty field' and route a retried all-empty recovery to `empties`), so every attempt-1/attempt-2 combination maps to exactly one counter.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.03,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A mapping so recovered whose 4 fields are all empty increments `empties` and degrades without retry.'","Plan: 'Only a reply from which no object carrying the field names can be recovered increments `digest_unparsed` and is retried once; a retry that succeeds counts as a success.'","Plan: 'A reply unrecoverable on BOTH attempts increments `digest_failed`.'","ABSENCE: the compound path unparsed-then-recovered-all-empty is enumerated by none of the three branches; 'succeeds' is not defined as 'recovers a non-empty mapping' vs 'recovers any mapping'."],"finding":"The digest retry state machine has no counter defined for the outcome 'attempt 1 unrecoverable (digest_unparsed, retried), attempt 2 recovers an object whose 4 fields are all empty'. That outcome is neither 'unrecoverable on BOTH attempts' (attempt 2 WAS recovered) nor a 'success', and the all-empty path (empties) is explicitly the no-retry path, so it is unreachable from a retry. The executor has no rule for which counter — if any — increments, and whether the ticket is left unvectored.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3e03dbf1780a2d2b","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Constraints → 'Digest step.' paragraph; AC lines 'An unrecoverable reply is retried once', 'A retry that succeeds counts as a success', 'Unrecoverable on both attempts increments digest_failed'.","norm_id":"nc81700a60689daae","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A nondeterministic model (ADR 0122 records exactly this: tickets that fail to answer the digest task, succeeding on retry) returns prose on attempt 1 and an empty-field object on attempt 2.","A test exercising the retry path cannot determine the expected final counter values or whether the ticket counts as vectored."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define the retry outcome space explicitly over both attempts: a retry 'succeeds' iff it recovers a mapping with at least one non-empty field (ticket indexes, no failure counter); a retried reply recovered but all-empty increments `empties` and leaves the ticket unvectored; only a reply from which no field-carrying object is recoverable on BOTH attempts increments `digest_failed`.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","citation [rebar:4e89-30b9-1666-4e53] ('**Both model choices are configuration, unset by default.** `[llm] embedding_mod') names no VERIFIED upstream prerequisite: P neither declares `depends_on -> 4e89-30b9-1666-4e53` nor is blocked by it. Add a `depends_on` edge to 4e89-30b9-1666-4e53, ensure 4e89-30b9-1666-4e53 `blocks` this ticket, or remove the citation. Until then the cited symbol is grounded as normal (fails closed)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State, per provider-failure arm, the disposition surfaced using an explicit disposition word: whether a timeout/throttle is treated as retryable/transient (and how that is preserved so a later build recovers) versus a denial treated as fatal/permanent, rather than collapsing both into one undifferentiated degrade.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Degrade means retrieval returns the lexical tier's whole-corpus results, the create advisory carries them, a diagnostic is emitted and create exits 0.'","AC12: 'A provider denial or timeout degrades. Test: parameterize both, assert status/advisory/diagnostic.' — denial (likely fatal/permanent) and timeout (likely transient/retryable) lumped into one disposition.","The plan uses no explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) for the provider-failure arm; rebar tokens like WAIT_AND_RETRY / classify_llm_failure / exit-11 are absent for this path."],"finding":"The plan adds a provider-failure fallback arm (degrade-to-lexical) and a retry-once arm, but AC12 collapses BOTH a provider denial AND a timeout into one undifferentiated 'degrades' outcome without stating each arm's disposition with an explicit disposition word. A transient throttle/timeout (retryable) and a permanent denial (fatal) are treated identically — silently degraded to lexical with create exiting 0 — so the plan never says whether the provider-failure arm's retryable leg is preserved (e.g. surfaced for a later build to recover) or masked by the fallback's exit-0 degrade. This is the 1c0d shape: a retryable primary failure masked by the fallback's own disposition.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6e0c266a30ee7a0d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Constraints 'Degrade means...' and AC12 'A provider denial or timeout degrades.'","norm_id":"n5b74d3605b27509e","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Split AC12's disposition: a transient provider failure (timeout/429) degrades THIS query to lexical but leaves the entry unvectored/retryable so a subsequent build_vectors recovers it (the retryable leg is preserved, not masked by the exit-0 degrade); a permanent denial is fatal for that provider's use until reconfigured. State this with disposition words in the Degrade constraint.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the embedding path obtains providers through the existing ProviderSession.provider_factory seam (credentials + tracked/closed httpx client), or justify why infer_embedding_model needs no provider_factory hook.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4969,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["providers.py:1-9: 'provider_factory, the (str)->Provider hook pydantic-ai's infer_model(provider_factory=...) calls ... the retrying httpx.AsyncClient a builder opens alongside it is tracked in self._closeables and closed on __exit__'","Plan: 'Its embeddings API (infer_embedding_model, Embedder, EmbeddingModel) dispatches a provider:model string in the shape providers.py already uses.'","ABSENCE: the plan names infer_embedding_model but not whether it accepts/uses the provider_factory hook, so credential construction and httpx-client close lifecycle for the embedding backend are unspecified."],"finding":"The plan does not specify how the existing provider-construction seam (ProviderSession.provider_factory, which supplies credentials and owns/closes the retrying httpx.AsyncClient) is wired into the embedding path; it only says infer_embedding_model dispatches a 'provider:model string in the shape providers.py already uses'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd5d3342b17153a68","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Constraints -> 'Vendor-neutrality uses a seam the runtime ships.'","norm_id":"n11fd7719ce904872","priority":0.1031,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A bedrock/openai embedding backend needs the same credential builder and retrying client the chat path gets, but infer_embedding_model is called with only a string","Per-run embedding httpx clients leak because nothing tracks them in ProviderSession._closeables"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence specifying that build_vectors resolves the embedder inside a ProviderSession so infer_embedding_model receives the same provider_factory hook (and its closeable client is tracked/closed), matching how llm/providers.py wires infer_model.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm (with a test) that infer_embedding_model resolves a model id containing an embedded colon (e.g. amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0) to the intended provider/model rather than mis-splitting it.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["config.py:147-152: 'a MODEL ID MAY ITSELF CONTAIN A COLON ... Reading such an id as provider:model yields a \"provider\" of ...'","split_provider_qualifier (config.py:218-221) partitions on ':' and only treats the prefix as a provider when it is a KNOWN provider name","Plan's own recommended value 'bedrock:amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0' has a trailing ':0' in the model id."],"finding":"The recommended embedding id 'bedrock:amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0' contains a colon inside the model id, and the repo already treats provider:model colon-splitting as a known hazard; the plan does not confirm the embedding dispatch preserves the embedded colon.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f63bbf2dca65bfb41","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Constraints -> 'Both model choices are configuration' / 'Vendor-neutrality uses a seam the runtime ships.'","norm_id":"n9a20d04098c2e2c8","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["infer_embedding_model naively splits on the first colon and mis-parses the titan model id, resolving the wrong model or raising"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact"